# Valgrind memcheck suppressions for the MPICH CI leg (ticket-018, R68/R73).
#
# Admission rule -- every entry in this file must satisfy all four:
#   1. Names an exact error kind (Memcheck:Param, Memcheck:Addr8, ...), never
#      a wildcard kind.
#   2. Has at least one `fun:` frame inside MPICH, UCX, libfabric, hwloc or
#      libc -- i.e. the report originates in a dependency, not in code this
#      project owns.
#   3. Never names a `ferrompi_*`, `rust_*` or example frame. A suppression
#      that hides such a frame would mask the very defects this job exists
#      to catch and must be rejected.
#   4. Never uses an `obj:` wildcard line naming a shared object instead of a
#      function; use `...` to elide frames instead, so a suppression stays
#      pinned to a named function, not "anything in this shared object".
#
# Entries are added only for reports observed on the CI MPICH job
# (Ubuntu 24.04's hotfixed libmpich12 4.2.1-5 + UCX, see
# .github/scripts/mpich-hotfix.sh) for the examples tagged `valgrind` in
# their `// mpi-test:` directive. Generate candidates with
# `--gen-suppressions=all` on a throwaway CI run, then copy in only the
# entries that satisfy the rule above.
#
# --leak-check is off (D-8: window memory leaks by design), so no entry here
# is a Leak suppression.
